& [FindingOne]
  + the initial journal digest renderer repeated the earlier unsupported attempt to apply uppercase-hex formatting directly to a SHA256 byte array
  + Rust rejected the formatter at compile time and no invalid digest reached a fixture or acceptance result
  + correction uses the same explicit bounded byte-wise uppercase hexadecimal encoding already proved in the P1 seam

& [FindingTwo]
  + one chain-refusal unit test attempted to hold an immutable link borrow while mutating the containing bundle
  + Rust rejected the overlapping borrow and the test was corrected by limiting the borrow scope and cloning only the bounded identity needed for the assertion
  + the correction changes test construction only and does not widen production acceptance semantics

& [RecurrenceControl]
  + later digest-bearing seams must reuse a shared reviewed hex encoder or the already published helper instead of reintroducing array formatting
  + compile failures are excluded from acceptance counts and remain durable even though the corrected focused suite passes

& [Verification]
  + twelve module two CLI and three independent static/integration tests pass after both corrections
  + controlled one-link two-link replay and three adversarial refusals pass with no Git process physical contact mutation dependency or provider activation

& [Frontier]
  + exact workspace gates evidence closure attribution publication and post-push bookend remain required
